# Architecture

Never rewrite a module that already exists unless the user explicitly asks. Extend it.

Do not add placeholder files, empty stubs, or unused folders.

Keep code modular. One concern per module. Routers stay thin.

This directory is the RecoveryPilot-AI project root. Follow that tree exactly.

## Folder structure (follow exactly)

```
apps/frontend/         # React + Vite + Tailwind + TypeScript
apps/backend/          # FastAPI app: main, api, models, schemas, core, db
services/              # all business logic
integrations/          # external APIs (Razorpay, WhatsApp, LLM, etc.)
shared/                # cross-cutting types and constants
simulator/             # batch recovery simulator
database/              # models, Alembic, Postgres init, seed scaffolding
docker/                # Dockerfiles and nginx
docs/                  # architecture notes
docker-compose.yml
```

Backend internals live under `apps/backend/app/` (`api/`, `models/`, `schemas/`, `core/`, `db/`). Do not put domain logic there.

```python
# ❌ BAD — logic in the router, HTTP in the service
@router.post("/recover")
def recover(payload: dict):
    return httpx.post("https://api.razorpay.com/...", json=payload).json()

# ✅ GOOD — router -> services/ -> integrations/
@router.post("/recover")
def recover(payload: RecoverRequest, db: Session = Depends(get_db)):
    return recovery_service.run(db, payload)
```
